---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro"
import Notice from "../components/Notice.astro"
import { components, componentHref, componentNumber, isNew } from "../lib/catalog"
---

<Docs
  title="Introduction"
  eyebrow="GPUI Kit"
  description="Editable shadcn visual ports backed by native GPUI behavior. Add the source you need, then own it in your application."
>
  <Notice />
  <div class="prose intro">
    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <p>
      gpuicn is a catalog of components for <a href="https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/main/crates/gpui">GPUI</a>,
      the GPU-accelerated UI framework behind Zed. Each component follows the shadcn/ui design and
      behaves like a native control: pointer, keyboard and accessibility activation come from GPUI Kit,
      not from a browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      You install components as source. <code>gpuicn add button</code> copies the Rust module into your
      app, where you can read it, change it and keep it. If you would rather depend on a crate, the
      <code>gpuicn</code> crate compiles the same registry and <code>gpuicn eject</code> turns any
      component back into editable source.
    </p>
    <h2>How to read a component page</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Preview</strong> runs the real component in your browser through WebAssembly.</li>
      <li><strong>Installation</strong> gives the command and the module declarations it maintains.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage</strong> is a compile-checked example to paste into a view.</li>
      <li><strong>API reference</strong> lists every public function from the installed source.</li>
      <li><strong>Platform notes</strong> record parity gaps and interaction limits on this GPUI revision.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <h2 class="h2 intro__catalog" id="components">Components</h2>
  <ol class="index">
    {
      components.map((component) => (
        <li class="index__item">
          <a class="index__link" href={componentHref(component.slug)}>
            <span class="index__num">{componentNumber(component.slug)}</span>
            <span class="index__name">{component.name}</span>
            <span>{isNew(component) && <span class="tag">New</span>}</span>
            <span class="index__desc">{component.description}</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</Docs>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .intro__catalog {
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header) + 1rem);
  }
</style>
